{"title":"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of these fractions is equivalent is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/2/d72c763982a2892bafcce5febd5ddf30d3a4f6c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/0/040be7d89cc95779e4cf39a533a7df48cf502f67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{3}{4} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{3}{5} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{5}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"371\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we can break <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> into their prime factors:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/e/42ecb6fe33233817abc30314d057da68dc44c9fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 = 3 \\times 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/a/43ad502bdd4cfa01433c768e02faa3e94fcfc9ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 = 5 \\times 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Thus:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/f/e8f769183b689e4496d536393b650358999139e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{25} = \\frac{3 \\times 5}{5 \\times 5} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } \\frac{3}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"176\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index